body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `projectionRows` function hardcodes `DEFAULT_PATHS.projectionIn` when recording diagnostics. If a custom path is passed to `buildPhaseBFull9709B0B1LocalRehearsalArtifacts`, any malformed/missing projection diagnostics will report the wrong path, which is misleading.

Additionally, if `projection` is `null` or `undefined` because `safeReadJson` failed to load/parse the file, pushing a redundant `projection_input_malformed` diagnostic is unnecessary and confusing.

We can resolve both issues by:
1. Adding a `projectionInPath` parameter to `projectionRows` defaulting to `DEFAULT_PATHS.projectionIn`.
2. Returning early without pushing a diagnostic if `projection` is `null` or `undefined` (since `safeReadJson` already handles and logs the load/parse failure).

```javascript
function projectionRows(projection, diagnostics = null, projectionInPath = DEFAULT_PATHS.projectionIn) {
  if (projection === null || projection === undefined) {
    return [];
  }
  if (typeof projection !== 'object' || Array.isArray(projection)) {
    diagnostics?.push(
      inputDiagnostic('projection_input_malformed', projectionInPath, 'projection input is not an object', {
        role: 'phase_b_full_9709_local_schema_projection_contract',
      }),
    );
    return [];
  }
  if (!Array.isArray(projection.rows)) {
    diagnostics?.push(
      inputDiagnostic('projection_rows_malformed', projectionInPath, 'projection rows is not an array', {
        role: 'phase_b_full_9709_local_schema_projection_contract',
      }),
    );
    return [];
  }
  return projection.rows;
}
```

